-- ccc7-s184-interception.l4 -- sections 184 (interception), 184.1 (interception to prevent bodily harm), 184.4 (immediate interception, imminent harm),
-- 184.5 (radio-based telephone communications) and 184.6 (one application for both kinds) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part VI.
-- (Sections 184.2 and 184.3 are in ccc7-s184-applications.l4.)
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against it.
--
-- HOW THE ANSWERS ARE READ (full statement in NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc7)").
-- An offence function (`s 184(1) the person is guilty ...`) answers the provision's own question: JUST TRUE (every element holds and no saving provision applies), JUST FALSE (an element is shown not to hold, or a saving
-- provision applies), NOTHING (an element or a saving limb turns on a term that is itself not covered). JUST FALSE is NOT a finding of innocence: it says this subsection does not make the conduct an offence.
-- A saving limb (`s 184(2)(a)` and so on) answers JUST TRUE when its facts hold ("Subsection (1) does not apply to"), JUST FALSE when its own conditions fail (marginal reading (a)), NOTHING when a borrowed term is not covered.
-- A grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12). Defined terms of section 183 are inputs of type MAYBE BOOLEAN named for the section ("by s 183 ..."): a caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Section 184 -- Interception (the offence, the saving provision, and use or retention)`

-- Plain gloss: using a device to listen in on a private communication, knowing you are doing so, is an offence, unless a saving limb of subsection (2) applies.
-- The two limbs of the penalty: on indictment, up to five years; or on summary conviction (no penalty is stated here: section 787(1) in another part supplies it, so its answer is an input).
-- src:3748 | Interception of Communications
-- src:3749 | Interception
-- src:3750 | 184 (1) Every person who, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, knowingly intercepts a private communication is guilty of
-- src:3751 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3752 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184(1) (src:3748-3752)
GIVEN `the person used an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the person did is intercepting, by s 183 intercept` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is a private communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 184(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 184(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, knowingly intercepts a private communication is guilty of"
        IF (`the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`subsection (1) does not apply to the person, by s 184(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): an element or the saving provision turns on a term that is not covered (an act "intercept includes" does not name, or a borrowed term)
    WHERE
        `the elements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST
                    `the person used an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`
                    , `what the person did is intercepting, by s 183 intercept`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person acted knowingly`
                    , `the communication is a private communication, by s 183`)

-- 184(1)(a): "an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years".
-- src:3751 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
@ref Criminal Code s 184(1)(a) (src:3751-3751)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 184(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`
                    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
                    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
                    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- 184(1)(b): "an offence punishable on summary conviction": the text states no penalty; the penalty is that of section 787(1) (ccc29), an input of type Punishment named for that section.
-- src:3752 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184(1)(b) (src:3752-3752)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 184(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- Both limbs, as the seam other parts ask for ("the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)"): ss 718.2, 718.3, 743.1, 463 to 465, 21 to 24.
-- src:3750 | 184 (1) Every person who, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, knowingly intercepts a private communication is guilty of
-- src:3751 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3752 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184(1) (src:3750-3752)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 184(1) the punishments` MEANS
    LIST `s 184(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`
        , `s 184(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- "is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction": the section gives both limbs, the Crown electing (hybrid: the word does not occur in the text).
-- src:3750 | 184 (1) Every person who, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, knowingly intercepts a private communication is guilty of
-- src:3751 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3752 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184(1) (src:3750-3752)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 184(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 184(2)(a): "a person who has the consent to intercept, express or implied, of the originator of the private communication or of the person intended by the originator thereof to receive it".
-- Section 183.1 adds that, where several persons originate or are to receive it, the consent of any one of them is sufficient consent for the purposes of any provision of this Part.
-- src:3753 | Saving provision
-- src:3754 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to
-- src:3755 | (a) a person who has the consent to intercept, express or implied, of the originator of the private communication or of the person intended by the originator thereof to receive it;
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(a) (src:3753-3755)
GIVEN `the person has the consent to intercept, express or implied, of the originator or of the person intended by the originator to receive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(a) the person has the consent to intercept` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has the consent to intercept, express or implied, of the originator or of the person intended by the originator to receive it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): whether the consent of one of several persons is sufficient consent is for section 183.1, whose answer is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person who has the consent to intercept, express or implied, of the originator of the private communication or of the person intended by the originator thereof to receive it"

-- 184(2)(b): "a person who intercepts a private communication in accordance with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4 or any person who in good faith aids in any way another person who
-- the aiding person believes on reasonable grounds is acting with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4". "Authorization" is the section 183 term; section 184.4 is in this module.
-- src:3756 | (b) a person who intercepts a private communication in accordance with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4 or any person who in good faith aids in any way another person who the aiding person believes on reasonable grounds is acting with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4;
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(b) (src:3756-3756)
GIVEN `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person intercepts in accordance with that instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intercepts pursuant to section 184.4, by s 184.4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person in good faith aids in any way another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aiding person believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(b) the person intercepts in accordance with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4, or aids a person who is` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the three routes` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the three routes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person who intercepts a private communication in accordance with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4 or any person who in good faith aids in any way another person who the aiding person believes on reasonable grounds is acting with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the instrument is an "authorization", or whether section 184.4 was satisfied, is not covered
    WHERE
        `the three routes` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued any of`
                (LIST
                    `s 183 three-valued all of`
                        (LIST `the instrument is an authorization, by s 183 authorization`
                            , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person intercepts in accordance with that instrument`)
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of`
                        (LIST `the person intercepts pursuant to section 184.4, by s 184.4`)
                    , `s 183 three-valued all of`
                        (LIST `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person in good faith aids in any way another person`
                            , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the aiding person believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4`))

-- 184(2)(c)(i): a person engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public who intercepts a private communication, if the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service.
-- src:3757 | (c) a person engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public who intercepts a private communication,
-- src:3758 | (i) if the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service,
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(c)(i) (src:3757-3758)
GIVEN `the person is engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(c)(i) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts as necessary to provide the service` MEANS
    IF `the person is engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` AND `the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service"

-- 184(2)(c)(ii): ... in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks.
-- src:3757 | (c) a person engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public who intercepts a private communication,
-- src:3759 | (ii) in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks, or
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(c)(ii) (src:3757-3759)
GIVEN `the person is engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interception is in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(c)(ii) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts in service observing or random monitoring` MEANS
    IF `the person is engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` AND `the interception is in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks"

-- 184(2)(c)(iii): ... if the interception is necessary to protect the person's rights or property directly related to providing the service.
-- src:3757 | (c) a person engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public who intercepts a private communication,
-- src:3760 | (iii) if the interception is necessary to protect the person’s rights or property directly related to providing the service;
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(c)(iii) (src:3757-3760)
GIVEN `the person is engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interception is necessary to protect the person’s rights or property directly related to providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(c)(iii) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts to protect their rights or property` MEANS
    IF `the person is engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public` AND `the interception is necessary to protect the person’s rights or property directly related to providing the service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the interception is necessary to protect the person’s rights or property directly related to providing the service"

-- 184(2)(c): any of (i), (ii) or (iii).
-- src:3757 | (c) a person engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public who intercepts a private communication,
-- src:3758 | (i) if the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service,
-- src:3759 | (ii) in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks, or
-- src:3760 | (iii) if the interception is necessary to protect the person’s rights or property directly related to providing the service;
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(c) (src:3757-3760)
GIVEN `s 184(2)(c)(i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 184(2)(c)(ii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 184(2)(c)(iii)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(c) a person providing a communication service to the public intercepts in one of the three ways` MEANS
    `s 183 three-valued any of` (LIST `s 184(2)(c)(i)` , `s 184(2)(c)(ii)` , `s 184(2)(c)(iii)`)

-- 184(2)(d): an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management, in respect of a private communication intercepted by that officer or servant for the purpose of
-- identifying, isolating or preventing an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission.
-- src:3761 | (d) an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management, in respect of a private communication intercepted by that officer or servant for the purpose of identifying, isolating or preventing an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission; or
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(d) (src:3761-3761)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication was intercepted by that officer or servant for the purpose of identifying, isolating or preventing an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(d) a spectrum management officer intercepts to identify, isolate or prevent an unauthorized use of a frequency` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management` AND `the communication was intercepted by that officer or servant for the purpose of identifying, isolating or preventing an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in respect of a private communication intercepted by that officer or servant for the purpose of identifying, isolating or preventing an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission"

-- 184(2)(e): a person, or any person acting on their behalf, in possession or control of a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2), who intercepts a private communication originating from, directed to or transmitting
-- through that computer system, if the interception is reasonably necessary for (i) managing the quality of service of the computer system ..., or (ii) protecting the computer system against any act that would be an offence
-- under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1). "Computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)" is another part's term: asked as an input, named for that section.
-- src:3762 | (e) a person, or any person acting on their behalf, in possession or control of a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2), who intercepts a private communication originating from, directed to or transmitting through that computer system, if the interception is reasonably necessary for
-- src:3763 | (i) managing the quality of service of the computer system as it relates to performance factors such as the responsiveness and capacity of the system as well as the integrity and availability of the system and data, or
-- src:3764 | (ii) protecting the computer system against any act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1).
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2)(e) (src:3762-3764)
GIVEN `the thing is a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person, or a person acting on their behalf, is in possession or control of the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication originates from, is directed to or transmits through that computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interception is reasonably necessary for managing the quality of service of the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interception is reasonably necessary for protecting the computer system against any act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2)(e) a person in control of a computer system intercepts as reasonably necessary to manage or protect it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the facts` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the interception is reasonably necessary for"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing is a "computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)" is for that subsection and is not covered
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `the thing is a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person, or a person acting on their behalf, is in possession or control of the computer system`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the communication originates from, is directed to or transmits through that computer system`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` (`the interception is reasonably necessary for managing the quality of service of the computer system` OR `the interception is reasonably necessary for protecting the computer system against any act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1)`))

-- 184(2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to" a person within any of (a) to (e): a flat negative. JUST TRUE if a limb holds; JUST FALSE if every limb fails on the facts (marginal reading (a): a failed condition of a limb is the text's no for that limb);
-- NOTHING if no limb holds and some limb is not covered.
-- src:3753 | Saving provision
-- src:3754 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to
-- src:3755 | (a) a person who has the consent to intercept, express or implied, of the originator of the private communication or of the person intended by the originator thereof to receive it;
-- src:3756 | (b) a person who intercepts a private communication in accordance with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4 or any person who in good faith aids in any way another person who the aiding person believes on reasonable grounds is acting with an authorization or pursuant to section 184.4;
-- src:3757 | (c) a person engaged in providing a telephone, telegraph or other communication service to the public who intercepts a private communication,
-- src:3758 | (i) if the interception is necessary for the purpose of providing the service,
-- src:3759 | (ii) in the course of service observing or random monitoring necessary for the purpose of mechanical or service quality control checks, or
-- src:3760 | (iii) if the interception is necessary to protect the person’s rights or property directly related to providing the service;
-- src:3761 | (d) an officer or servant of Her Majesty in right of Canada who engages in radio frequency spectrum management, in respect of a private communication intercepted by that officer or servant for the purpose of identifying, isolating or preventing an unauthorized or interfering use of a frequency or of a transmission; or
-- src:3762 | (e) a person, or any person acting on their behalf, in possession or control of a computer system, as defined in subsection 342.1(2), who intercepts a private communication originating from, directed to or transmitting through that computer system, if the interception is reasonably necessary for
-- src:3763 | (i) managing the quality of service of the computer system as it relates to performance factors such as the responsiveness and capacity of the system as well as the integrity and availability of the system and data, or
-- src:3764 | (ii) protecting the computer system against any act that would be an offence under subsection 342.1(1) or 430(1.1).
@ref Criminal Code s 184(2) (src:3753-3764)
GIVEN `s 184(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 184(2)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 184(2)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 184(2)(d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 184(2)(e)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb turns on a term or an authorization that is not covered
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 183 three-valued any of` (LIST `s 184(2)(a)` , `s 184(2)(b)` , `s 184(2)(c)` , `s 184(2)(d)` , `s 184(2)(e)`)

-- 184(3): "A private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e) can be used or retained only if (a) it is essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system; or
-- (b) it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2)." "only if" closes the list: neither (a) nor (b) is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3765 | Use or retention
-- src:3766 | (3) A private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e) can be used or retained only if
-- src:3767 | (a) it is essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system; or
-- src:3768 | (b) it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 184(3) (src:3765-3768)
GIVEN `the communication was intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2), by s 193(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(3) a private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e) can be used or retained` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the communication was intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private communication intercepted by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(e)"
        IF `it is essential to identify, isolate or prevent harm to the computer system`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2), by s 193(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is to be disclosed in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2), by s 193(2)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the disclosure is in circumstances referred to in subsection 193(2) is for that subsection and is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "can be used or retained only if"

§ `Section 184.1 -- Interception to prevent bodily harm`

-- 184.1(4) agent of the state means (a) a peace officer; and (b) a person acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer. FORK (F7): "and" joins two kinds of agent (a union), not two requirements on one person.
-- src:3778 | Definition of agent of the state
-- src:3779 | (4) For the purposes of this section, agent of the state means
-- src:3780 | (a) a peace officer; and
-- src:3781 | (b) a person acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.1(4) (src:3778-3781)
GIVEN `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.1(4) agent of the state` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 183 three-valued any of` (LIST `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person is acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 183 three-valued any of` (LIST `the person is a peace officer, by s 2 peace officer` , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the person is acting under the authority of, or in cooperation with, a peace officer`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "agent of the state means"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): whether the person is a peace officer is for section 2 "peace officer", which says "includes" and is not covered

-- 184.1(1): "An agent of the state may intercept, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, a private communication if (a) either the originator ... or the person intended ... has consented to the interception;
-- (b) the agent of the state believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented to the interception; and (c) the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm."
-- A grant named "may" with an "if" gate: a failed gate is NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12; fork line F8 gives the other reading).
-- src:3769 | Interception to prevent bodily harm
-- src:3770 | 184.1 (1) An agent of the state may intercept, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, a private communication if
-- src:3771 | (a) either the originator of the private communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception;
-- src:3772 | (b) the agent of the state believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented to the interception; and
-- src:3773 | (c) the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.1(1) (src:3769-3773)
GIVEN `the person is an agent of the state, by s 184.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the interception is by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the communication is a private communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `either the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent of the state believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented to the interception` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.1(1) an agent of the state may intercept a private communication` MEANS
    IF `s 183 three-valued all of`
           (LIST `the person is an agent of the state, by s 184.1(4)`
               , `the interception is by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`
               , `the communication is a private communication, by s 183`
               , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `either the originator or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception`
               , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the agent of the state believes on reasonable grounds that there is a risk of bodily harm to the person who consented to the interception`
               , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the purpose of the interception is to prevent the bodily harm`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if (a) either the originator of the private communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it has consented to the interception"

-- 184.1(2): the contents of a private communication obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1) "are inadmissible as evidence except for the purposes of proceedings in which actual, attempted or threatened bodily harm
-- is alleged, including proceedings in respect of an application for an authorization under this Part or in respect of a search warrant or a warrant for the arrest of any person." The function is named for the bar: JUST TRUE = inadmissible.
-- src:3774 | Admissibility of intercepted communication
-- src:3775 | (2) The contents of a private communication that is obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1) are inadmissible as evidence except for the purposes of proceedings in which actual, attempted or threatened bodily harm is alleged, including proceedings in respect of an application for an authorization under this Part or in respect of a search warrant or a warrant for the arrest of any person.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.1(2) (src:3774-3775)
GIVEN `the contents of a private communication were obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are ones in which actual, attempted or threatened bodily harm is alleged, including proceedings in respect of an application for an authorization under this Part or in respect of a search warrant or a warrant for the arrest of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.1(2) the contents are inadmissible as evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contents of a private communication were obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The contents of a private communication that is obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1)"
        IF `the proceedings are ones in which actual, attempted or threatened bodily harm is alleged, including proceedings in respect of an application for an authorization under this Part or in respect of a search warrant or a warrant for the arrest of any person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purposes of proceedings in which actual, attempted or threatened bodily harm is alleged"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 184.1(3): "The agent of the state who intercepts a private communication pursuant to subsection (1) shall, as soon as is practicable in the circumstances, destroy any recording ..., any full or partial transcript of the recording and any
-- notes made by that agent of the private communication if nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur."
-- The duty, as a decision function: JUST TRUE = bound to destroy; JUST FALSE = the "if nothing ... suggests" condition fails (a duty whose "if" is unmet: fork F9); NOTHING = the agent did not intercept pursuant to (1).
-- src:3776 | Destruction of recordings and transcripts
-- src:3777 | (3) The agent of the state who intercepts a private communication pursuant to subsection (1) shall, as soon as is practicable in the circumstances, destroy any recording of the private communication that is obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1), any full or partial transcript of the recording and any notes made by that agent of the private communication if nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.1(3) (src:3776-3777)
GIVEN `the agent of the state intercepted a private communication pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.1(3) the agent of the state is bound to destroy the recording, transcript and notes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the agent of the state intercepted a private communication pursuant to subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The agent of the state who intercepts a private communication pursuant to subsection (1)"
        IF `nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur"

-- Whether the duty of 184.1(3) has been kept: JUST TRUE = bound and destroyed as soon as is practicable in the circumstances; JUST FALSE = bound and not destroyed as soon as is practicable ("shall");
-- NOTHING = not bound on the facts, or whether the agent is bound is not covered. "As soon as is practicable in the circumstances" has no number: it is a plain fact the agent states.
-- src:3776 | Destruction of recordings and transcripts
-- src:3777 | (3) The agent of the state who intercepts a private communication pursuant to subsection (1) shall, as soon as is practicable in the circumstances, destroy any recording of the private communication that is obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1), any full or partial transcript of the recording and any notes made by that agent of the private communication if nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.1(3) (src:3776-3777)
GIVEN `s 184.1(3) bound` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the agent destroyed all of them as soon as is practicable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.1(3) the agent of the state has kept the duty to destroy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 184.1(3) bound` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN IF `the agent destroyed all of them as soon as is practicable in the circumstances`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, as soon as is practicable in the circumstances, destroy"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty binds only the agent who intercepted pursuant to subsection (1) and only if nothing in the communication suggests bodily harm

-- The same duty as a regulative rule (no period is stated: "as soon as is practicable in the circumstances", so no WITHIN).
DECLARE `s 184.1(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 184.1(3) destroys the recording, every transcript and the notes`

-- src:3776 | Destruction of recordings and transcripts
-- src:3777 | (3) The agent of the state who intercepts a private communication pursuant to subsection (1) shall, as soon as is practicable in the circumstances, destroy any recording of the private communication that is obtained from an interception pursuant to subsection (1), any full or partial transcript of the recording and any notes made by that agent of the private communication if nothing in the private communication suggests that bodily harm, attempted bodily harm or threatened bodily harm has occurred or is likely to occur.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.1(3) (src:3776-3777)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 183 party under Part VI` `s 184.1(3) act`
`s 184.1(3) the duty to destroy as a rule` MEANS
    PARTY `s 183 an agent of the state`
    MUST `s 184.1(3) destroys the recording, every transcript and the notes`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 183 an agent of the state` BECAUSE "s 184.1(3): the recording, transcripts and notes were not destroyed as soon as was practicable"

§ `Section 184.4 -- Immediate interception: imminent harm`

-- 184.4: "A police officer may intercept, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, a private communication if the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that (a) the urgency of the situation is such that
-- an authorization could not, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under any other provision of this Part; (b) the interception is immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or to property; and
-- (c) either the originator ... or the person intended ... is the person who would commit the offence that is likely to cause the harm or is the victim, or intended victim, of the harm."
-- A grant named "may" with an "if" gate: a failed gate is NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12; fork line F8).
-- src:3828 | Immediate interception — imminent harm
-- src:3829 | 184.4 A police officer may intercept, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, a private communication if the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:3830 | (a) the urgency of the situation is such that an authorization could not, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under any other provision of this Part;
-- src:3831 | (b) the interception is immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or to property; and
-- src:3832 | (c) either the originator of the private communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it is the person who would commit the offence that is likely to cause the harm or is the victim, or intended victim, of the harm.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.4 (src:3828-3832)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer, by s 183 police officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the interception is by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the communication is a private communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the urgency of the situation is such that an authorization could not, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under any other provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the interception is immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or to property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the originator or the intended recipient is the person who would commit the offence or is the victim, or intended victim, of the harm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.4 a police officer may intercept a private communication` MEANS
    IF `s 183 three-valued all of`
           (LIST `the person is a police officer, by s 183 police officer`
               , `the interception is by means of an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`
               , `the communication is a private communication, by s 183`
               , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the urgency of the situation is such that an authorization could not, with reasonable diligence, be obtained under any other provision of this Part`
               , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the interception is immediately necessary to prevent an offence that would cause serious harm to any person or to property`
               , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the originator or the intended recipient is the person who would commit the offence or is the victim, or intended victim, of the harm`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the police officer has reasonable grounds to believe that"

§ `Section 184.5 -- Interception of radio-based telephone communications`

-- 184.5(1): "Every person who intercepts, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, maliciously or for gain, a radio-based telephone communication, if the originator of the communication or the person
-- intended by the originator of the communication to receive it is in Canada, is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- Section 184.5(2) brings the saving provision of 184(2) to this offence: its answer, as it applies by 184.5(2), is the input.
-- src:3833 | Interception of radio-based telephone communications
-- src:3834 | 184.5 (1) Every person who intercepts, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, maliciously or for gain, a radio-based telephone communication, if the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it is in Canada, is guilty of
-- src:3835 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3836 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.5(1) (src:3833-3836)
GIVEN `the person used an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the person did is intercepting, by s 183 intercept` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acted maliciously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted for gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is a radio-based telephone communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 184(2) does not apply to the person, as it applies by s 184.5(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.5(1) the person is guilty of an offence under the subsection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection 184(2) does not apply to the person, as it applies by s 184.5(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 183.1, subsection 184(2) and sections 184.1 to 190 and 194 to 196 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require"
        IF `the elements` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who intercepts, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, maliciously or for gain, a radio-based telephone communication, if the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it is in Canada, is guilty of"
        IF (`the elements` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`subsection 184(2) does not apply to the person, as it applies by s 184.5(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): an element or the saving provision turns on a term that is not covered
    WHERE
        `the elements` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST `the person used an electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, by s 183`
                    , `what the person did is intercepting, by s 183 intercept`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` (`the person acted maliciously` OR `the person acted for gain`)
                    , `the communication is a radio-based telephone communication, by s 183`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator to receive it is in Canada`)

-- src:3834 | 184.5 (1) Every person who intercepts, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, maliciously or for gain, a radio-based telephone communication, if the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it is in Canada, is guilty of
-- src:3835 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
@ref Criminal Code s 184.5(1)(a) (src:3834-3835)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 184.5(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`
                    `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
                    `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
                    `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                    `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:3836 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.5(1)(b) (src:3836-3836)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 184.5(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3834 | 184.5 (1) Every person who intercepts, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, maliciously or for gain, a radio-based telephone communication, if the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it is in Canada, is guilty of
-- src:3835 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3836 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.5(1) (src:3834-3836)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 184.5(1) the punishments` MEANS
    LIST `s 184.5(1)(a) the punishment on indictment`
        , `s 184.5(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3834 | 184.5 (1) Every person who intercepts, by means of any electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device, maliciously or for gain, a radio-based telephone communication, if the originator of the communication or the person intended by the originator of the communication to receive it is in Canada, is guilty of
-- src:3835 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:3836 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.5(1) (src:3834-3836)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 184.5(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 184.5(2): "Section 183.1, subsection 184(2) and sections 184.1 to 190 and 194 to 196 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to interceptions of radio-based telephone communications referred to in subsection (1)."
-- A list of provisions that is not closed with "only": a provision outside it is NOT COVERED. Section numbers are decimals, so "sections 184.1 to 190" includes 184.2 to 184.6, 185, 186, 186.1, 187, 188, 188.1, 188.2, 189 and 190,
-- and "194 to 196" includes 195 and 196 but not 196.1, which is numbered after 196 (fork F10, and finding 4 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3837 | Other provisions to apply
-- src:3838 | (2) Section 183.1, subsection 184(2) and sections 184.1 to 190 and 194 to 196 apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, to interceptions of radio-based telephone communications referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Criminal Code s 184.5(2) (src:3837-3838)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the interception is of a radio-based telephone communication referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.5(2) the provision applies to the interception` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the interception is of a radio-based telephone communication referred to in subsection (1)`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to interceptions of radio-based telephone communications referred to in subsection (1)"
        IF provision's `section` EQUALS 183.1
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (provision's `section` EQUALS 184) AND (provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (provision's `section` AT LEAST 184.1) AND (provision's `section` AT MOST 190)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (provision's `section` AT LEAST 194) AND (provision's `section` AT MOST 196)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the list names the provisions that apply; it does not say that no other provision applies

§ `Section 184.6 -- One application for authorization sufficient`

-- 184.6: "For greater certainty, an application for an authorization under this Part may be made with respect to both private communications and radio-based telephone communications at the same time."
-- src:3839 | One application for authorization sufficient
-- src:3840 | 184.6 For greater certainty, an application for an authorization under this Part may be made with respect to both private communications and radio-based telephone communications at the same time.
@ref Criminal Code s 184.6 (src:3839-3840)
GIVEN `the application is for an authorization under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made with respect to both private communications and radio-based telephone communications at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184.6 one application for an authorization may be made for both kinds of communication` MEANS
    IF `the application is for an authorization under this Part` AND `it is made with respect to both private communications and radio-based telephone communications at the same time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application for an authorization under this Part may be made with respect to both private communications and radio-based telephone communications at the same time"
